-- title:
--   Surjectivity after base change descends to a f.g. subalgebra
-- statement:
--   Let $R$, $A$, $D$, $C$ be commutative rings in a single universe, with $A$, $D$, $C$ all $R$-algebras, and let $\varphi \colon D \to C$ be an $R$-algebra homomorphism whose underlying ring homomorphism is of finite type, i.e. $C$ is generated as a $D$-algebra (via $\varphi$) by finitely many elements. Assume that the base-changed map $\mathrm{id}_A \otimes \varphi \colon A \otimes_R D \to A \otimes_R C$ is surjective as a function, and let $s$ be a finite subset of $A$. Then there exists an $R$-subalgebra $T \subseteq A$ which is finitely generated (`T.FG`, i.e. $T$ is the $R$-subalgebra generated by some finite subset of $A$), contains $s$ as a subset of $A$, and is such that the base-changed map $\mathrm{id}_T \otimes \varphi \colon T \otimes_R D \to T \otimes_R C$ is already surjective.
--
--   This is the standard Noetherian-approximation statement that surjectivity of a finite-type algebra map after base change to a filtered union is detected at a finitely generated stage, in the algebraic form used to approximate closed immersions. It is cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion.exists_fg_subalgebra_of_isClosedImmersion_pullback_map`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion.exists_fg_subalgebra_of_isClosedImmersion_pullback_map).
